    "updated_at": "2021-11-17T14:58:25Z",
    "body": "I'm not facing a problem myself, just worried about code like:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nenterFullscreen.addEventListener('pointerdown', () => {\r\n  fullscreenElement.requestFullscreen();\r\n});\r\n```\r\n\r\nWith the current definition, this will work fine when tested with mouse as we have defined that pointerdown triggers activation if the pointerType is 'mouse'. However, it will fail when used with touch or pen because we don't activate until the pointerup event for those input types.\r\n\r\nIt also sounds like [WebKit had compat issues trying to remove activation on touchstart / pointdown with pointerType == 'touch'](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/3849#issuecomment-941529191), so I imagine they'd be unlikely to implement the current proposal, and that many sites are relying on touchstart having activation today.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
